# Build context for the broker image (Dockerfile). An allowlist: the image
# needs the workspace manifests, the lockfile and two packages, nothing else.
#
# Without this file the whole checkout is sent to the daemon — every
# node_modules (gigabytes, and on Windows full of junctions that don't survive
# the trip), the apps, the videos, and a root .env holding real keys — and a
# host-built services/broker/node_modules would be copied over the Linux one
# the image just installed.
*
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!.npmrc
!tsconfig.base.json
!packages/protocol/
!services/broker/

# Re-excluded inside the allowed packages: host installs and builds (the image
# makes its own), tests, and anything that looks like a secret or local state.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/test
**/coverage
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/data
**/*.db
